<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">dragon-lord</ansi>

The Dragon Lord is the neutral elite of the Dragon Tamer (Beast Tamer route;
no alignment asked). Its drake grows larger, its Breath leaves foes burning
and reaches four foes, and the first Breath comes in the first round.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Ranks</ansi>

  30 Searing breath     foes the drake's Breath strikes are left alight (2
                        damage a round for 4 rounds)
  35 Greater drake      the drake has 150% of a wolf's health
  40 Dragonfire         +4 damage on the drake's bites and its Breath (in all)
  45 Wide breath        Breath reaches four foes
  50 Drake ascendant    the drake has 180% of a wolf's health
  55 Razor claws        +4 Attack on the drake's bites
  60 Furnace heart      the drake's first Breath comes in the battle's first
                        round

It needs the Dragon Tamer first (<ansi fg="command">help beasttamer-routes</ansi>) and keeps every rank of it. At level 30 a
character that holds it promotes with <ansi fg="command">class promote [member] dragon-lord confirm</ansi>. Any alignment may take it.
Everything here lasts only for the battle and is never saved.

<ansi fg="yellow-bold">Elite talents</ansi>

Elite Beast Tamer talents (levels 35, 45, 55): Iron Hide (+5 Armor), Pack
Bond (your beast has 15% more health), Savage Jaws (+2 damage on your
beast's blows). See <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.

See also: <ansi fg="command">help beasttamer-routes</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help beasttamer</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help elite</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help promotion</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help talents</ansi>.
